    "https://jobs.wrexham.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=2627103": {
      "title": "Careers and Employability Assistant",
      "description": "2627103 Careers and Employability Assistant - Jobs at Wrexham Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use Study Student life International Business Connect Research About Home Login Register Cymraeg Toggle Menu This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Job Vacancies 2627103 Careers and Employability Assistant Careers and Employability Assistant The Careers and Employability Service at Wrexham University is seeking to appoint a Careers and Employability Assistant to support the delivery of high-quality bilingual careers services and employability activity. The role requires the effective use of both Welsh and English to provide comprehensive bilingual administrative support, ensuring the effective delivery of University careers and employability services. Welsh language skills are essential for this role Performing a variety of duties and practical tasks arising from the planning, promotion and delivery of transformative careers and employability activity, you will work closely with the Head of Careers and Employability to enhance services and support for students and graduates. The successful candidate will be able to maintain and develop sustainable, efficient office systems and processes using a range of digital platforms, including Microsoft 365, Target Connect, Power BI, Moodle, LinkedIn Learning, University finance systems and the Service’s social media channels. Based at the Wrexham Campus, with activity delivered across all physical and digital locations, the Careers and Employability Service is a core part of the University’s learning and teaching activity and the overall student experience. Wrexham University is a forward-thinking, student-focused institution, recognised as one of the most equitable universities in the UK, with a strong emphasis on learning and teaching quality, student outcomes and graduate success. Please see the Job Description for full details of the position. If you would like further information, please contact Lucy Jones, Head of Careers and Employability, at Lucy.Jones@wrexham.ac.uk . Further details Job Description - Welsh Job Description - English Email details to a friend Apply Online Wrexham University is an equal opportunities employer and positively encourages applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates and will ensure applicants will not be discriminated against due to their protected characteristics under the Equality Act 2010. The University will make all efforts to meet your access requirements. Please contact our People Team as soon as possible to discuss any adjustments or assistance you may need to complete your application form, or to answer any queries you may have. We welcome applications in Welsh and English. Any applications submitted in Welsh will not be treated less favourably than applications submitted in English. Excellence, Inclusion, Collaboration, Transformation & Sustainability Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Programme/Department Careers and Employability Location Wrexham Salary £26,701\r\n              per annum Post Type Full Time Closing Date Sunday 25 October 2026 Reference 2627103 Welsh Language Skills Welsh language skills are essential Apply Online Jobs at Wrexham Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Job Notifications Jobs by Email Study with us Undergraduate courses Postgraduate courses Short courses Online Courses Apply Quick Links Contact Us