      "title": "Sport Science Technician Demonstrator",
      "description": "2627107 Sport Science Technician Demonstrator - Jobs at Wrexham Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use Study Student life International Business Connect Research About Home Login Register Cymraeg Toggle Menu This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Job Vacancies 2627107 Sport Science Technician Demonstrator Sport Science Technician Demonstrator We are seeking an enthusiastic and technically skilled Technician Demonstrator in Sport Science to support the delivery of teaching, research, and practical activities across our laboratory and field environments. The role will involve supporting students and staff in the safe and effective use of specialist sport science equipment, including Cortex Metalyser, Qualisys, VALD and Isokinetic Dynamometer systems. You will be responsible for maintaining, calibrating, and troubleshooting high-end instrumentation to ensure optimum performance and reliability. You will also manage laboratory bookings, maintain safe and functional laboratory environments, and ensure compliance with health and safety requirements, including the preparation of risk assessments and COSHH documentation. Essential Criteria BSc (Hons) in Sport and Exercise Science or a relevant sport-related discipline or relevant work experience. Specialist knowledge and practical skills in biomechanics and exercise physiology. Experience working with sport science laboratory equipment and instrumentation. Strong understanding of laboratory health and safety procedures. Excellent organisational, communication, and practical problem-solving skills. Further details Job Description - Welsh Job Description - English Email details to a friend Apply Online Wrexham University is an equal opportunities employer and positively encourages applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates and will ensure applicants will not be discriminated against due to their protected characteristics under the Equality Act 2010. The University will make all efforts to meet your access requirements. Please contact our People Team as soon as possible to discuss any adjustments or assistance you may need to complete your application form, or to answer any queries you may have. We welcome applications in Welsh and English. Any applications submitted in Welsh will not be treated less favourably than applications submitted in English. Excellence, Inclusion, Collaboration, Transformation & Sustainability Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Programme/Department Sport Location Wrexham Salary £29,588 to £33,951\r\n              per annum Post Type Full Time Closing Date Tuesday 13 October 2026 Reference 2627107 Welsh Language Skills Welsh language skills are desirable Apply Online Jobs at Wrexham Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Job Notifications Jobs by Email Study with us Undergraduate courses Postgraduate courses Short courses Online Courses Apply Quick Links Contact Us Open days Virtual tours Online Shop Welcome Week Academic Timetable Staff & Students Student Portal Staff Portal Job Vacancies Contact Wrexham University, Mold Road, Wrexham, LL11 2AW 01978 290666 We welcome calls in Welsh or English. Rydym yn croesawu galwadau yn Gymraeg neu Saesneg. Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok © Wrexham University Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use"
