    "https://jobs.wrexham.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=2627133": {
      "title": "Principal Lecturer in Cyber & Computing",
      "description": "2627133 Principal Lecturer in Cyber & Computing - Jobs at Wrexham Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use Study Student life International Business Connect Research About Home Login Register Cymraeg Toggle Menu This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Job Vacancies 2627133 Principal Lecturer in Cyber & Computing Principal Lecturer in Cyber & Computing The Faculty of Arts, Computing and Engineering is seeking to appoint a Principal Lecturer to lead our high performing Cyber and Computing subject area for an 18 month fixed term period. This is an exciting opportunity to provide operational and academic leadership for an established subject area with a strong recent record of student experience and National Student Survey performance. Working closely with the Dean, Associate Deans and wider Faculty leadership team, the post holder will play a key role in maintaining academic excellence while supporting the continued development and strategic direction of Cyber and Computing. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with Principal Lecturers across the Faculty and wider University to identify opportunities, share effective practice and contribute to the delivery of the University’s 2030 Strategy. Central to the role will be an understanding of the future development of Cyber and Computing and the ability to translate strategic priorities into effective operational delivery. The post holder will be expected to make effective use of available resources, manage competing priorities and draw upon information from multiple sources to support evidence informed decision making. Excellent communication, collaborative leadership and relationship management skills are essential. The successful candidate will lead and support an established academic team, creating a positive and collegiate environment in which colleagues can contribute effectively to subject, Faculty and University objectives. Applications are welcomed from colleagues who can demonstrate leadership and influence, including leadership without formal portfolio responsibility. The role involves oversight of a diverse and complex portfolio of activity, including UK and international provision, traditional and online delivery, transnational education and academic partnerships. Applicants should therefore be able to demonstrate the organisational skills and adaptability required to manage activity across different modes and contexts. We particularly welcome applications from colleagues who can demonstrate experience and leadership across learning and teaching innovation, academic quality, subject research, partnerships, innovation and enterprise. The role will also contribute to the continued development of the Cyber Innovation Academy, working collaboratively with regional schools, colleges, employers and industry partners to strengthen progression and talent pipelines, develop external engagement and support opportunities for third stream income. The post holder will have line management responsibility for staff within Cyber and Computing and will report to an Associate Dean. The ability to communicate through the medium of Welsh is desirable for this post. Interviews are currently scheduled to take place early November 2026. Further details Job Description - Welsh Job Description - English Email details to a friend Apply Online Wrexham University is a signatory to the Researcher Development Concordat and Research Integrity Concordat. The University is committed to the principles of these concordats and is dedicated to the development of researchers in all posts and upholding the highest standards of rigour and integrity in all aspects of research. Wrexham University is an equal opportunities employer and positively encourages applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates and will ensure applicants will not be discriminated against due to their protected characteristics under the Equality Act 2010. The University will make all efforts to meet your access requirements. Please contact our People Team as soon as possible to discuss any adjustments or assistance you may need to complete your application form, or to answer any queries you may have. We welcome applications in Welsh and English. Any applications submitted in Welsh will not be treated less favourably than applications submitted in English. Excellence, Inclusion, Collaboration, Transformation & Sustainability Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Programme/Department Cyber and Computing Location Wrexham Salary £58,225 to £67,468\r\n              per annum Post Type Full Time Fixed Term Until Friday 29 September 2028 Closing Date Sunday 25 October 2026 Reference 2627133 Welsh Language Skills Welsh language skills are desirable Apply Online Jobs at Wrexham Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Job Notifications Jobs by Email Study with us Undergraduate courses Postgraduate courses Short courses Online Courses Apply Quick Links Contact Us Open days Virtual tours Online Shop Welcome Week Academic Timetable Staff & Students Student Portal Staff Portal Job Vacancies Contact Wrexham University, Mold Road, Wrexham, LL11 2AW 01978 290666 We welcome calls in Welsh or English. Rydym yn croesawu galwadau yn Gymraeg neu Saesneg. Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok © Wrexham University Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use"
