      "title": "Sessional Lecturer",
      "description": "SESS-NUTRITIONDIETETICS Sessional Lecturer - Nutrition and Dietetics - Jobs at Wrexham Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use Study Student life International Business Connect Research About Home Login Register Cymraeg Toggle Menu This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Job Vacancies SESS-NUTRITIONDIETETICS Sessional Lecturer - Nutrition and Dietetics Sessional Lecturer - Nutrition and Dietetics The Nutrition & Dietetics team at Wrexham University is seeking to develop a pool of Sessional Lecturers to support delivery of our undergraduate Nutrition & Dietetics programme, preparing students for professional, person-centred practice. We are looking for enthusiastic individuals with relevant professional expertise and experience of teaching and learning. Sessional Lecturers may contribute to a range of activities including: Lesson planning and preparation Teaching and facilitation of learning activities Assessment and feedback Student support and guidance Contributing to an excellent student learning experience Applicants should be able to engage and support learners effectively and work collaboratively within an academic team. Support required will vary according to operational need throughout the academic year. By joining our sessional lecturer pool, you may be contacted when opportunities arise to contribute to programme delivery. Current registration with a relevant professional body and experience within healthcare, nutrition, dietetics or higher education is required. If you are passionate about supporting the development of future healthcare professionals and would like to contribute to Nutrition & Dietetics education at Wrexham University, we would be delighted to hear from you. Email details to a friend Apply Online Wrexham University is an equal opportunities employer and positively encourages applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates and will ensure applicants will not be discriminated against due to their protected characteristics under the Equality Act 2010. The University will make all efforts to meet your access requirements. Please contact our People Team as soon as possible to discuss any adjustments or assistance you may need to complete your application form, or to answer any queries you may have. We welcome applications in Welsh and English. Any applications submitted in Welsh will not be treated less favourably than applications submitted in English. Excellence, Inclusion, Collaboration, Transformation & Sustainability Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Programme/Department Nutrition & Dietetics Location Wrexham Salary per hour Post Type Casual Closing Date Sunday 18 October 2026 Reference SESS-NUTRITIONDIETETICS Welsh Language Skills Welsh language skills are desirable Apply Online Jobs at Wrexham Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Job Notifications Jobs by Email Study with us Undergraduate courses Postgraduate courses Short courses Online Courses Apply Quick Links Contact Us Open days Virtual tours Online Shop Welcome Week Academic Timetable Staff & Students Student Portal Staff Portal Job Vacancies Contact Wrexham University, Mold Road, Wrexham, LL11 2AW 01978 290666 We welcome calls in Welsh or English. Rydym yn croesawu galwadau yn Gymraeg neu Saesneg. Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok © Wrexham University Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use"
